-- title:
--   Dominant indices at interior depth: finite and nonempty
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e \ge 1$. Let $q \ge 1$ be a scaling integer. Consider the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\varpi^{e})$, the quotient of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ (as `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`) by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e}$, and let $x$ be a nonzero element of it. Let $ab = (a,b)$ be a pair of one-variable power series over $W$ with $b$ of zero constant coefficient, such that $x$ is the class of $\mathrm{inU}\,a + \mathrm{inV}\,b$, where $\mathrm{inU}\,a$ is the series with coefficient $a_{d_0}$ at an exponent $d$ with $d_1 = 0$ and $0$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{inV}\,b$ has coefficient $b_{d_1}$ at $d$ with $d_0 = 0$ and $0$ otherwise. Let $p$ be a natural number with $1 \le p$ and $p + 1 \le qe$. Write $v(w) = q \cdot \mathrm{addVal}_W(w) \in \mathbb{N} \cup \{\infty\}$ for $q$ times the normalised additive valuation. Then the set of $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $$v(\mathrm{nfCoeff}\ ab\ n) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\ (qe)\ p\ (\mathrm{nfExponent}\ n) \;=\; \inf_{d}\ \bigl(v(\mathrm{coeff}_d(\mathrm{inU}\,a + \mathrm{inV}\,b)) + \mathrm{annulusWeight}\ (qe)\ p\ d\bigr),$$ the infimum being over all exponents $d : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to_{f} \mathbb{N}$, is both finite and nonempty.
--
--   This is the basic finiteness statement for the dominant terms of an element of the width-$e$ crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^{e})$ on a circle of strictly interior rational depth $p/q$ in the annulus $0 \le v(U) \le e$: nonemptiness rests on $x \ne 0$, and finiteness on $0 < p < qe$ (at the endpoints infinitely many indices can be dominant). It is used in the interior slope law for the Gauss order, namely by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.slopeDrop_sub_eq_circleIndexDrop_sub_of_forall_circleIndexDrop_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.slopeDrop_sub_eq_circleIndexDrop_sub_of_forall_circleIndexDrop_eq), so that the supremum and infimum of the dominant index set are attained.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_dominantIndices_finite_nonempty.lean

